  "description": "Just a few quick stock market notes",
  "body_html": "<p>Stock Market Update: 💩</p><p>LOL, jokes aside, the broader market is not doing anything of note. I only had a few positions remaining after our <a href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/stock-market-warning-signal?r=4z8lgl\">September 30<sup>th</sup> sell off</a>, many of the positions light. The primary focus right now is to <em><strong>protect all the 2025 profits</strong></em>. That means not buying dips, not dollar cost averaging, not picking up new positions until the market proves otherwise. <a href=\"https://substack.com/@stocktok/note/c-173918064?r=4z8lgl&amp;utm_source=notes-share-action&amp;utm_medium=web\">Yesterdays Video</a> remains 100% relevant…no body knows where the bottom is at…so don’t try to time it! Early October “buy the dip” geniuses have had a terrible month.</p><p><strong>DO NOT RUN AWAY THOUGH</strong>…opportunities always seem to arise when the general public has given up hope. If you had a bad trade, welcome to the club. 👋 The best investors in the world have bad days. I have bad days. It’s normal. Cut the loss, learn from it, and move on! <strong>Keep losses small, and your winners big!</strong> We will have stocks to play, at some point…I can’t tell you when, as I’ll recognize it when I see it. </p><p>A few quick notes on my positions:</p><ul><li><p><span class=\"cashtag-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;symbol&quot;:&quot;$CLSK&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CashtagToDOM\"></span> <strong>cut</strong> today for a loss. This position was light from the start, so not a huge deal…though disappointing nonetheless.</p></li><li><p>Bright Springs Health, <span class=\"cashtag-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;symbol&quot;:&quot;$BTSG&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CashtagToDOM\"></span> is well into <strong>profit</strong>, but I will not allow anything below $31.90, to guarantee profits with it. This is a position we compounded the win with. </p></li><li><p><span class=\"cashtag-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;symbol&quot;:&quot;$IWM&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CashtagToDOM\"></span> is still within consolidation range. It moves pretty slowly (usually). So I am not concerned about it at the moment. We started an initial position at $249.80. Just <strong>monitor</strong>ing. </p></li><li><p><span class=\"cashtag-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;symbol&quot;:&quot;$NFLX&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CashtagToDOM\"></span> <em><strong>short</strong></em> is <strong>in profit</strong>. Risk has been <em><strong>reduced</strong></em>. Broader trends are carrying it though, for the time being. Reminder: if you short, <strong>ALWAYS</strong> use a stop. Short squeezes are real, and they can suck.  </p></li><li><p><span class=\"cashtag-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;symbol&quot;:&quot;$AISP&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CashtagToDOM\"></span> Was up 22% for us…then proceeded to retest its entire consolidation range 🙄. I am a human being, and do regret not following my own “quick pump” rule: If stock spikes &gt;20% in a day, take it. Live and learn. I mentioned at the beginning, this stock was a penny stock, could range up to +/-60%, and still be in a bull trend. This is the nature of a $142M market cap. If you are over invested…that is on you…Ive preached about position sizing relentlessly this year, and even built a tool to help you calculate position sizing. </p></li></ul><p>So overall, still very light in the market (I am more than 95% cash). If you do not know me, and you’re thinking “these stocks suck”… you are correct. When positions are working for us, I can get up to ~15ish stocks, and then I add to those as they trend upwards. For example, we dollar cost averaged UP on <span class=\"cashtag-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;symbol&quot;:&quot;$RGTI&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CashtagToDOM\"></span> twice during its euphoric run; <span class=\"cashtag-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;symbol&quot;:&quot;$RBLX&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CashtagToDOM\"></span> wins were compounded 3x on its 61% run. Start light, build positions as they work. <strong>They are not working right now, so just relax!   </strong></p><p>Some other notes:</p><ul><li><p>Many people trade and invest regularly from the <a href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/stocktok-summary?r=4z8lgl\">StockTok Screener</a>. This is a screener that meets rigorous requirements to identify the strongest momentum stocks. <strong>Bloom Energy, <span class=\"cashtag-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;symbol&quot;:&quot;$BE&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CashtagToDOM\"></span> was the biggest winner to date, at +395%</strong>. The first signal came on July 9th when it was $28.55. It now trades at $142 a share. This was the first bull market the screener was active. It turns off during periods of high volatility; most screeners are useless because they erase wins with losses in bear markets. Mine will flat out turn off in less optimal conditions. I am reviewing all of the winning stocks, and figuring ou<strong>t: “what did the biggest winners have in common?”</strong>. The thought process is that in the next bull cycle (yes, we need to go into a bear cycle, at least for a while) we will be able to identify the biggest winners early on. We caught a nice profit with BE, but certainly not 395%.  </p></li><li><p>I am also working on reverse engineering a Volatility Contraction Pattern (VCP) indicator. This is an incredibly tough indicator to build. I do not want it for TradingView. I want to build a Python screener, that searches 5000+ tickers for those set ups. Stay tuned for updates on that. </p></li></ul><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!1aIv!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F96e4f53b-8ec2-4933-b0c8-f7714118c026_4128x2052.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset